# Wide Test - TWIDE, a TEST course (SPEC.md 130.54.8): the BZDEV=1 build's alone, after the shipped courses (the
# Makefile's BZ_TESTCRS), on no pad, with no shipped demo.  "The far east": the one course at the widest width
# a course may have, 160 word columns (1,280 px, SPEC.md 130.10.4.2), so the rows that read the map walk a
# part whose map row is neither 64 nor 128 words (bz_mrow, 130.10.4.2) -
#  - one RIBBON along +x (wx 12 - 75, five cells deep), so it runs DOWN the picture to the east: a = wx - wy
#    from -32 to 35, the cell centres px 96 - 1,168, with its back rail and an END WALL at wx 76.  It runs
#    diagonally, not straight across, so no block row holds more than 128 occluder records in ANY of the
#    tool's compiles (SPEC.md 130.11.4.2): a straight east-west ribbon across 140 word columns puts a record
#    in nearly every one of them in a single block row once the AV model is off (the selfcheck's `av`
#    section prices AV against that compile, and refused the first TWIDE's 140);
#  - the route from the west end to the GOAL, the ribbon's last column, by its back corner (75, 40): the
#    autopilot rides the whole width, so the camera scrolls to its eastmost window (CGA c0 120, Hercules
#    115) and the entering columns are the last;
#  - an EAST MARKER (twide_east.bba) in the last word columns, 155 - 159, beside the goal;
#  - the STEEL ball, the tool's limit, the finish clock beside the goal.
course TWIDE "Wide Test"
test             # SPEC.md 130.54: a test course - no pad, no shipped demo, no target owed
music fairway    # SPEC.md 130.50.3: every course names its song
width 160
origin 608        # x0: the reach from px 8 (a = -36) to 1,271 (a = 40)
ball steel
floor rect  12 40 76 45  flat 4            # the ribbon, along +x
wall  rect  12 39 76 40  flat 12           # its back rail
wall  rect  76 40 77 45  flat 12           # the END WALL, the picture's far east
goal  rect  75 40 76 45  flat 4            # the goal, the ribbon's east end
start 14 42
way 14 42
way 40 42
way 75 40
clock 70 44                                # the finish clock (SPEC.md 130.22.6)
art twide_east.bba 1244 600               # the EAST MARKER: ink in word columns 155 - 159, beside the goal
